 "asked_at": "2026-10-16T01:13+08:00",
 "answer": "I can't get a live reading. The pages I found are cached snapshots from different times, so treat these numbers as approximate. They do agree on one thing: Penang's air quality is **Moderate**, with PM2.5 as the main pollutant.\n\n| Source / location | AQI | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| IQAir – George Town | 92 US AQI, Moderate, PM2.5 at 31 µg/m³ | Snapshot from 13:00 on Oct 15 |\n| IQAir – Bukit Mertajam | 58 US AQI, Moderate, PM2.5 at 12.9 µg/m³ | Snapshot from 10:00 on Oct 13 |\n| IQAir – Permatang Kuching | 55 US AQI, Moderate, PM2.5 at 11.2 µg/m³ | Snapshot from 20:00 on Oct 12 |\n| IQAir – Butterworth | 63 US AQI, Moderate, PM2.5 at 15.5 µg/m³ | Snapshot from 14:00 on Oct 7 |\n| Weather Underground – Penang | AQI 68, Moderate, dominant pollutant PM2.5 | Date not shown |\n| AccuWeather – Penang Airport | AQI 67 | Snapshot from Oct 7 |\n\n**What \"Moderate\" means:** People with respiratory issues should reduce prolonged or heavy outdoor exertion. For most people, normal outdoor activity is fine.\n\n**Differences between areas:** George Town's reading was the highest of the snapshots, at 92. The other areas were mostly in the 50s and 60s. Levels vary by location and by time of day.\n\nFor a current number, check [IQAir's Penang page](https://www.iqair.com/air-quality/malaysia/penang/george-town). Malaysia's Department of Environment also publishes the official API readings on its MyAQI site.",
